  "raw": "\nA TRICKY little brainteaser is strongly implying that Mama Dragons are all hiding eggs.\nAnd the hide and seek challenge on social media platform Hinge has challenged Aussie users to spot it.\n2 The dragon lies encased by cushion Credit: Twitter\nThe image shows the dragons melded together with one tucked under another's back like mud sticks onto trees, whilst others perched on mobile read apps.\nIncredulity surrounds the question, only four dragons have made an appearance compared to around a score of 50 mentions of 'Mama'.\nBut there could be more dragons than those who show up.\nThat's because the word 'mage' which is used into over 150 words like hmm hello where did this come from, icewinds etc means 'mummy' as in South Africa, 'mediaeval fantasy' \"Mancellany\", Italy, Portugal or Spain meaning young woman half his age \"Magritterie\" (from 1689",
